      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Natchaug State Forest dominates Eastford, offering hiking, horseback riding, fishing, and camping amid classic New England woods.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.ct.one/towns/eastford",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Phoenixville grew around a twine mill on the Still River in the early 1800s, now a quiet crossroads with historic houses.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.ct.one/towns/eastford",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Union Society of Phoenixville House, listed on the National Register, stands as a local landmark.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.ct.one/towns/eastford",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A monument in Eastford honors Nathaniel Lyon, the first Union general killed in the Civil War.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
